{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAFc2THvfEJnUdQnQnLs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The fix is in place and all tests pass, but it isn't committed: git has no author name or email set in this environment, so the commit failed.\n\n**What changed:** Panicking with `http.ErrAbortHandler` is the standard way to abort a request without logging, and Go's own HTTP server stays quiet when it sees it. Gin's recovery middleware was catching it as a crash, logging a full stack trace and running the 500 handler. Now `recovery.go:71` treats it the same way gin already treats a broken pipe:\n- It logs one line (the error and the request) with no stack trace.\n- It records the error on the context and aborts.\n- It doesn't call the 500 handler or a custom recovery handler, and keeps any status already set.\n\nI also added `TestPanicWithAbortHandler` in `recovery_test.go`. It checks that the status the handler set stays in place, the error message is logged, and no \"panic recovered\" stack dump appears.\n\n**One design choice:** recovery handles this panic instead of passing it on. Passing it on would let Go's server abort the connection, which is what `ErrAbortHandler` is meant to do, but it would skip gin's other middleware. Say if you'd prefer that.\n\nThe changes are on a new branch, `fix/recover-abort-handler`. To commit, set your git name and email and run:\n```\ngit commit -am \"fix(recover): suppress http.ErrAbortHandler in recover\"\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":488,"cache_read_input_tokens":34622,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":488,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bff18184-75af-405f-8877-a1cf5626aa63","uuid":"3f21ace9-6cbd-4a75-9ced-452f9fe10a9b","timestamp":"2026-10-18T19:26:51.278Z","request_id":"req_011CgAFc2F9cX15KvYtz6HaR"}
